From 867dd782e955db6f863db2708108b8dd2a929a8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ManicardiMatteo87 <manicardi.matteo87@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:14:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/19] diag(bms): D2 read-only UART2 line levels per DALY poll
 period (candidate)

For the DALY silences that start with a reply cut mid-frame (15/11 cold
capture) the existing D1 counters cannot tell what the ESP pins see during
the silence. D2 samples, in DalyBms::update(), UART2's status register
(status.rxd, status.txd, status.rxfifo_cnt; one load, no side effect) and
counts per poll period: samples, RX low, RX edges, TX low with an empty TX
FIFO at least 12 ms after the request, RX hardware FIFO not empty and its
maximum. Published at the next request as a trailing @BMS STATUS line and
bms_d2_* keys in /status. No bus traffic, no register write, nothing feeds
availability, health, LED or Motion power. Loop-rate snapshots of the ESP
side only: sustained levels, never short pulses or the RS485 bus.
Host test (test_daly_async: D2 accounting, no extra TX) and guard parser
test (trailing line inert). Diagnostic candidate, not flashed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 8429bc061975edd30794b1b5c9441e175f9ffbb6)
